     1	# ReluxNIOSSH rebase procedure
     2
     3	1. Start from a clean disposable worktree. Do not rebase in a product checkout
     4	   with unrelated changes.
     5	2. Record the candidate upstream tag/commit and download its commit archive.
     6	3. Run the conflict preflight against every upstream file currently patched:
     7
     8	   ```sh
     9	   python3 scripts/reluxniossh-fork-tool.py conflict-test \
    10	     --upstream-ref <candidate-tag-or-commit>
    11	   ```
    12
    13	   Exit `0` means none of the patched upstream files changed since the current
    14	   pin. Exit `1` lists the files requiring semantic review; it must not be
    15	   bypassed.
    16	4. Replace the fork tree with the verified candidate archive, preserving its
    17	   license and attribution. Reapply the five logical patches from
    18	   `RELUX_DELTA.md` in order. Never carry an old hunk solely to make a diff apply.
    19	5. Update `UPSTREAM.md` and `PATCH_MANIFEST.json` with the new tag, commit,
