   148	## Security
   149
   150	This product hides tunneled destinations, DNS, and payloads from the on-path
   151	network — but the exit host you choose sees your post-exit traffic, and a
   152	long-lived SSH session is fingerprintable as SSH. It is **not** an anonymity or
   153	DPI-evasion tool. Read [`.spec/threat-model.md`](.spec/threat-model.md) for the
   154	full does-hide / does-not-hide matrix and residual-risk register.
     1	# Contributing
     2
     3	## Before changing the product
     4
     5	1. Read `.spec/README.md` and `docs/current-state.md`.
     6	2. Install the project-management tooling using `docs/project-management.md`.
     7	3. Find or create the board element before implementation.
     8	4. Use `task-board` for every `.task-board/` mutation; do not edit board files by
     9	   hand.
    10	5. Link the relevant `.spec/` documents to the task as precondition resources.
    11	6. Do not implement VPN work until the generated plan has explicit user approval.
    12
    13	Changes that alter protocol, security, privacy, entitlements, routing, failure
    14	modes, or supported platforms must update the corresponding specification and
    15	`.spec/decisions.md`.
    16
    17	Native binary changes must also update `NativeDependencies/manifest.json`, be
    18	reproducible from pinned source, regenerate third-party notices, and pass
    19	`make validate-native`. Unpinned or runtime-downloaded native binaries are not
    20	accepted.
    21
    22	## Development baseline
    23
    24	The generated v2 application targets macOS 15.0 and uses a Swift tools 6.1
    25	package with Swift 6 language mode. The independently preserved legacy v0.1.0
    26	application remains on macOS 14.0, Swift tools 5.10, and Swift 5. Use the exact
    27	clean-checkout prerequisites and matrix in
    28	[`docs/generated-workspace-foundation.md`](docs/generated-workspace-foundation.md).
    29
    30	```sh
    31	make core-test
    32	make core-build
    33	```
    34
    35	The planned multi-target VPN has additional gates in `.spec/validation.md`.
    36	Passing current SwiftPM tests does not validate the future Network Extension.
    37
    38	This development Mac is build-only. Local build, compile, lint, unit,
    39	integration, harness, and unsigned-provider tests are allowed. Never install a
    40	system extension or containing app, save or remove a real VPN preference, call
    41	`startVPNTunnel`, activate a provider, or mutate host routes or DNS here.
    42	Physical macOS VPN work must be dependency-gated by `TASK-260819-25e1ys`, run
    43	on a separately provisioned Mac, and pass
    44	`scripts/physical-test-host-preflight.sh`. See
    45	[`docs/build-host-safety.md`](docs/build-host-safety.md).
    46
    47	## Commits and pull requests
    48
    49	- Keep commits focused and do not mix generated build output with source/docs.
    50	- Use the configured Ivan Oparin identity and signed commits for this repository.
    51	- Never commit signing certificates, App Store Connect keys, SSH private keys,
    52	  passphrases, provisioning secrets, tokens, or captured user traffic.
    53	- Include board element IDs and human-readable names in implementation pull
    54	  request descriptions once execution begins.
    55	- Report verification commands and any untested physical-device requirement.
    56	- Do not add AI attribution or `Co-Authored-By` trailers.
    57
    58	## Generated and local state
    59
    60	`.agents/`, `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.local/`, `.temp/`, build output, and local
    61	credentials are machine-local. `.task-board/`, `.planning/`, `.spec/`, and
    62	durable `.research/` evidence are source-controlled.

